list-set-overdraw

`ListState::set_overdraw` changes how much is laid out beyond the visible
area after construction. Dragging a scrollbar thumb across a long list lands
somewhere new every frame, and laying out rows nobody sees there was most of
the frame; the editor sets none while its thumb is held. Lists that never
call it behave as before.

